WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.009 --> 00:00:02.210
Waldorf Education is a holistic,

1
00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:06.920
child-centered approach developed by Rudolf Steiner in the early 20th century.

2
00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:09.159
Waldorf integrates intellectual,

3
00:00:09.289 --> 00:00:10.010
artistic,

4
00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:11.449
and practical learning.

5
00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.779
Designed to nurture the whole child,

6
00:00:13.989 --> 00:00:14.409
head,

7
00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:14.930
heart,

8
00:00:14.949 --> 00:00:15.789
and hands,

9
00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:19.739
Waldorf aligns instruction with distinct developmental stages.

10
00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:22.829
Early childhood focuses on imaginative play,

11
00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:23.549
rhythm,

12
00:00:23.709 --> 00:00:27.129
and sensory exploration without early academic pressure.

13
00:00:27.389 --> 00:00:28.690
In the elementary years,

14
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.500
learning is driven by the arts,

15
00:00:30.709 --> 00:00:31.250
music,

16
00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:32.250
storytelling,

17
00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:32.830
and movement.

18
00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:35.750
With students creating their own illustrated main

19
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.819
lesson books rather than using traditional textbooks.

20
00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:39.900
By high school,

21
00:00:40.029 --> 00:00:41.909
the focus shifts to critical thinking,

22
00:00:42.389 --> 00:00:43.419
independent analysis,

23
00:00:43.509 --> 00:00:44.900
and ethical reasoning.

24
00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.150
By connecting academic subjects through

25
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.299
creative expression and natural rhythms,

26
00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.630
Waldorf aims to cultivate creative,

27
00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:52.529
confident,

28
00:00:52.549 --> 00:00:54.110
and lifelong learners.